Id: crk001w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: crack_run
Fix: Have each account set a strong password; add pam_pwquality so weak ones cannot return.
References: pam_pwquality(8)
Controls: CIS 5.2; NIST IA-5(1); ISO 5.17; CE User access control

The Crack password guesser ran against the password file and guessed
somebody's password; the login ids follow the message. A guessable
password falls to the first dictionary an attacker tries. Make each
listed account pick a strong password, and consider a password-quality
check so weak ones cannot be set again.
